WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.915 --> 00:00:04.748
(engine starting)

00:00:06.343 --> 00:00:09.259
- [Voiceover] I never had money,

00:00:09.259 --> 00:00:13.044
so if I wanted anything, I'd
have to build it myself.

00:00:13.044 --> 00:00:16.544
I want other people to be able to do that.

00:00:19.573 --> 00:00:23.972
My name is Matthew McEntegart,
I own Vaydor Bodykits.

00:00:23.972 --> 00:00:26.628
We have a unique design
car that looks like

00:00:26.628 --> 00:00:28.876
a million dollars and we produce it so

00:00:28.876 --> 00:00:30.399
that the average person can build it

00:00:30.399 --> 00:00:32.355
for an affordable price.

00:00:32.355 --> 00:00:34.772
The best way to call this is a re-body.

00:00:34.772 --> 00:00:37.672
(drilling sound)

00:00:37.672 --> 00:00:40.675
You're making a new car
out of an existing car.

00:00:40.675 --> 00:00:42.859
We're cutting everything
off and what we're left with

00:00:42.859 --> 00:00:44.371
is just bare bones.

00:00:44.371 --> 00:00:48.316
The motor, the drive train,
the frame of the car.

00:00:48.316 --> 00:00:50.267
So you have all of your dashboard intact,

00:00:50.267 --> 00:00:52.971
all of your engine intact, all wiring,

00:00:52.971 --> 00:00:57.755
it's just the cosmetics that
have been cut off the car.

00:00:57.755 --> 00:01:00.172
My whole life I always
fixed up my own cars,

00:01:00.172 --> 00:01:02.899
so then I decided I'm just
gonna design my own car

00:01:02.899 --> 00:01:06.875
that I can call my own, it
doesn't look like anything else.

00:01:06.875 --> 00:01:09.460
I'm extremely excited that
a car that I designed,

00:01:09.460 --> 00:01:13.582
the Vaydor, is gonna be used
in the Suicide Squad movie.

00:01:13.582 --> 00:01:15.953
I had built a car for a customer

00:01:15.953 --> 00:01:17.387
on the other coast of Florida.

00:01:17.387 --> 00:01:19.860
While it was there the
production company walked in

00:01:19.860 --> 00:01:21.652
and they said that's great, it's perfect,

00:01:21.652 --> 00:01:22.820
you know, it looks like a million dollars

00:01:22.820 --> 00:01:25.238
and nobody's seen it before.

00:01:25.238 --> 00:01:28.093
I think that it ties in to Suicide Squad

00:01:28.093 --> 00:01:30.893
because it's threatening
when it drives down the road,

00:01:30.893 --> 00:01:33.976
it's an angular, open-mouth, angry car.

00:01:37.236 --> 00:01:38.723
Seeing my own design on the big screen

00:01:38.723 --> 00:01:41.574
is really exciting to me.

00:01:41.574 --> 00:01:44.741
The easiest way to put it
is, it's a lottery ticket.

00:01:44.741 --> 00:01:46.987
I wanted to design a super car.

00:01:46.987 --> 00:01:50.356
I can't draw, I have no design experience,

00:01:50.356 --> 00:01:53.667
so I've just shaped it out of foam.

00:01:53.667 --> 00:01:57.924
And it took me a year and
a half, seven days a week

00:01:57.924 --> 00:02:00.841
before I had a car out of the mold.

00:02:02.564 --> 00:02:06.259
I literally had nothing
when I finished this.

00:02:06.259 --> 00:02:10.036
Whatever money I had went
into developing this.

00:02:10.036 --> 00:02:12.515
It was pretty much the
biggest chance I've ever taken

00:02:12.515 --> 00:02:15.308
and this one just, it’s,
people love the car.

00:02:15.308 --> 00:02:18.579
It couldn't have worked out better.

00:02:18.579 --> 00:02:21.162
(upbeat music)

